{"name":"Apple II Beige","hex":"#bfca87","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"apple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A common, firm, round fruit produced by a tree of the genus Malus.","The fruit of the tree Malus domestica, chiefly with a green, red, or yellow skin, cultivated in temperate climates for cidermaking, cooking, and eating. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make (something) appear like an apple (noun sense 1.1).","To become like an apple.\n\n To collect fir-cones.\n Of a flower bud or vegetable (especially a root vegetable): to grow into the shape of an apple."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apple"},{"term":"beige","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour, variously defined from a pale brown, to a yellow greyish off-white.","Debeige; a kind of woollen or mixed dress goods."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a slightly yellowish gray colour, as that of unbleached wool.","Comfortably dull and unadventurous, in a way that suggests middle-class suburbia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beige"}],"entries":[{"title":"Apple II","blocks":[{"text":"The Apple II is a series of microcomputers manufactured by Apple Computer, Inc. from 1977 to 1993. The original Apple II model, which gave the series its name, was designed by Steve Wozniak and was first sold on June 10, 1977. Its success led to the Apple II Plus, Apple IIe, Apple IIc, and Apple IIc Plus, with the IIe being the most popular. The name is trademarked with square brackets as apple ][, then beginning with the IIe in 1983 as Apple //."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Apple_II-IMG_7064.jpg/330px-Apple_II-IMG_7064.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple_II","wikidata":"Q201652"},{"title":"Apple","blocks":[{"text":"An apple is the round, edible fruit of an apple tree. Fruit trees of the orchard or domestic apple, the most widely grown in the genus, are cultivated worldwide. The tree originated in Central Asia, where its wild ancestor, Malus sieversii, is still found. Apples have been grown for thousands of years in Eurasia before they were introduced to the American continent by European colonists. Apples have cultural significance in many mythologies and religions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Pink_lady_and_cross_section.jpg/330px-Pink_lady_and_cross_section.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple","wikidata":"Q89"},{"title":"Beige","blocks":[{"text":"Beige is variously described as a pale sandy fawn color, a grayish tan, a light-grayish yellowish brown, or a pale to grayish yellow. It takes its name from French, where the word originally meant natural wool that has been neither bleached nor dyed, hence also the color of natural wool."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Saint_Anthony_church_in_Chamboret_07.jpg/330px-Saint_Anthony_church_in_Chamboret_07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beige","wikidata":"Q843607"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Apple_iie.jpg/500px-Apple_iie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Apple_iie.jpg/500px-Apple_iie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Apple IIe with DuoDisk and Monitor //","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AApple_iie.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Apple_IIc_with_monitor.jpg/500px-Apple_IIc_with_monitor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/w